% TRIO, middle part, bars 185-208 (c003: 24 bars; v03 bars 189-196 cut).
% c022: 200 Ob 2 D sharp, Cl 1 B sharp: no fifths/octaves from iv to V; 203 viola D sharp: no fifths E-A/F sharp-B with the bass (A-S PDF 189-190).
% 185-192: call and response: Ob 1 in C sharp minor (185); the cellos, doubled an octave up by the cor anglais, answer a step lower, in B major (189).
%
% 193-200: the strings together, crescendo to the trio's forte: the oboe's call in C sharp minor in Vln I and II, ending on G sharp (V of C sharp).
% 201-208: A major, then A minor (mixture, iv), to the dominant pedal B; T's head in Cl 1 and Fl 1, diminuendo; the 7th A on the last beat (V7) falls to G sharp at 209.

% c032: 196-197 V7-vi: the 7th A only in Cl 1 (violas B, not A), Cl 1 A -> G# and Cl 2 D# -> E (the clarinet parts 197-200 exchanged an octave), so the 7th falls
%   and the leading tone rises into the deceptive C sharp minor (A-S PDF 76, 202).
% c033: 207-208 crescendo in the B-pedal parts, the timpani roll and the motto-tail line (Fl 1, Cl 1), so T's forte return at 209 is reached, not dropped in
%   after pp (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 127, amplification: the second group enters soft and crescendos faster; PDF 130, crescendo strings - wood - brass).
% c034: 197-200 Fl 1 doubles Vln I's E6 call at the trio's forte (Adler II PDF 151-152: the flute alone carries the top octave; Mozart 40/iv, Beethoven 9/i).
tBFluteOne = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | e'''4(\f dis'''8 cis'''8 dis'''8 e'''8 | cis'''2 gis''4) | a''4.( b''8 cis'''4) | gis''2.\> | R2.\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | gis''2(\pp a''4 | b''2.~ | b''2\< ais''4 | a''2.) | }
tBFluteTwo = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | cis''2.\f | cis''2. | cis''2. | bis'2.\> | R2.\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
% c023: 206-209 Fl 1 and Cl 1 hold B, then A sharp (207, beat 3) and A (208, the V7's 7th) to G sharp at 209: the motto's tail B-A sharp-A-G sharp,
%   at the pitch of Hn 1's close (coda), leads into T's return (A&S PDF 600-602: Mozart K. 542 quotes and enlarges the same B-A sharp-A-G sharp).
% c021: the calls at 185, 189 and 197 open with a quaver turn, so the trio's middle part does not repeat T's rhythm (2-4 | 2-4 | 4.-8-4 | 2.) a fifth to eighth time
tBOboeOne = { e''4(\p dis''8 cis''8 dis''8 e''8 | cis''2 gis'4) | a'4.( b'8 cis''4) | gis'2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | e''4(\f dis''8 cis''8 dis''8 e''8 | cis''2 gis'4) | a'4.( b'8 cis''4) | gis'2.\> | R2.\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
tBOboeTwo = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | gis'2.\f | gis'2. | fis'2. | dis'2.\> | R2.\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
tBCorAnglais = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | dis'4(\p cis'8 b8 cis'8 dis'8 | b2 fis4) | gis4.( a8 b4) | fis2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
tBClOne = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | a'2.\p\< | cis''2. | b'2. | a'2. | gis'2.\f | gis'2. | a'2. | gis'2.\> | \partCombineSoloII R2.\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | \partCombineAutomatic gis'2(\p a'4 | b'2.~ | b'2\< ais'4 | a'2.) | }
tBClTwo = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | fis'2.\p\< | fis'2. | e'2. | dis'2. | e'2.\f | e'2. | cis'2. | bis2.\> | e'2.\p | e'2. | dis'2.\> | dis'2. | dis'2.\! | dis'2. | dis'2.\< | dis'2. | }
tBBsnOne = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | a2.\p\< | a2. | gis2. | fis2 r4 | gis2.\f | gis2. | fis2. | bis,2.\> | cis'2.\p | c'2. | b2.\> | a2. | fis2.\! | fis2. | fis2. | fis2. | }
tBBsnTwo = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | cis2.\f | cis2. | fis,2. | gis,2.\> | a,2.\p | a,2. | b,2. | b,2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
tBHnOne = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | gis'2.\f | gis'2. | a'2. | gis'2.\> | R2.\! | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
